WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.620
Hollywood was once very niiiiiice to Sacha
Baron Cohen, the British comedian who broke

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:10.210
through in the U.S. with 2006’s Borat: Cultural
Learnings of America for Make Benefit Glorious

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.210
Nation of Kazakhstan.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.940
"Welcome to our country."

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:13.970
"My name ah Borat."

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:15.270
"Ok, well, ah good good.

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:17.420
I'm not used to that but that's fine"

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:22.440
Centered around an often crude, sexist, racist
and naïve reporter from Kazakhstan, the comedy

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:27.130
opened up opportunities for Cohen to star
in a wide range of big movies like Talladega

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:32.400
Nights, The Dictator, Alice Through the Looking
Glass, Les Misérables and more.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.739
But despite that string of roles, Baron Cohen
hasn't popped up on the big screen quite as

00:00:36.739 --> 00:00:40.739
often as he once did — and here are a few
reasons why.

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:41.739
Family man

00:00:41.739 --> 00:00:46.899
Unlike many of his peers, Baron Cohen doesn't
churn out multiple movies per year, and that's

00:00:46.899 --> 00:00:47.899
by design.

00:00:47.899 --> 00:00:52.429
Sacha and his wife, actress Isla Fisher, have
three young children, and they both want to

00:00:52.429 --> 00:00:54.239
be active, present parents.

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:58.100
Cohen has committed to only making a movie
every couple of years, while Fisher plans

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.249
to only take supporting role until their kids
are fully grown.

00:01:01.249 --> 00:01:04.860
While these Hollywood parents love to act,
it sounds like they're putting family first

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.799
— at least for a little while.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:08.250
Real World Reputation

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:13.049
Even if Baron Cohen wanted to keep making
reality-blurring movies like Borat, he doesn't

00:01:13.049 --> 00:01:14.049
think he could.

00:01:14.049 --> 00:01:18.729
A victim of his own success, he fears he's
become too recognizable to pull off a movie

00:01:18.729 --> 00:01:20.850
like Borat or Bruno again.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:24.579
On top of that, there's also the matter of
the inherent danger in making those kinds

00:01:24.579 --> 00:01:29.070
of movies, as Baron Cohen’s films have definitely
landed him in hot water in the past.

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:35.790
"The idea of the movie was actually to end
it with inciting a riot in Arkansas while

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.009
me and my co-star made out on stage."

00:01:38.009 --> 00:01:43.120
He was lucky to get out of that one unharmed,
but even a minor, non-deadly stunt from Sacha

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.880
can end up being very stressful.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.969
When Baron Cohen made a surprise appearance
as Ali G at the 2016 Academy Awards, people

00:01:49.969 --> 00:01:54.179
were genuinely shocked — because the show
producers had specifically told him not to

00:01:54.179 --> 00:01:55.179
do it.

00:01:55.179 --> 00:01:58.619
This caused some stress for his wife, who
had to be complicit in the prank and even

00:01:58.619 --> 00:02:02.540
smuggled the Ali G costume into the awards
ceremony under her dress.

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:06.820
She then had to help her husband get into
character backstage and lie to the producers

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:08.650
who were trying to figure out what he was
up to.

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:12.010
"So I was really stressed I was like 'Honey
honey this isn't gonna work' then I had to

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:15.540
go out finally and I said 'There is something
that is wrong with his stomach.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:16.540
It's really bad.'

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:21.090
Fisher did what any reasonable person would
do after faking out 20 million people on live

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:22.800
TV; she hit the bar...

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.370
The Brothers Grimsby

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:28.700
Baron Cohen's last "big" movie was 2016's
The Brothers Grimsby.

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:33.110
Like some of Baron Cohen's previous films,
the mismatched spy comedy made headlines not

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:36.590
for its creativity, but more for it’s shockingly
crude moments.

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:41.980
The movie was wildly unsuccessful, both commercially
and critically as it really seems like almost

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:43.930
no one connected with this flick.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:48.210
It was one of Baron Cohen's few leading roles
in a movie in which he didn't play a character

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:53.010
interacting with real life people — and
audiences just weren’t that into it.

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:54.010
One hit Wonder...

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:59.860
Between 2000 and 2004, Sacha Baron Cohen created
three main characters for his comedy series,

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:03.620
Da Ali G Show — Ali G, Borat and Bruno.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:07.250
And by 2009, he’d brought all of them to
the big screen.

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:12.920
While Ali G Indahouse wasn't released theatrically
in the U.S., 2006’s Borat was a massive

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:18.320
hit, bringing in $128 million and earning
Baron Cohen and his collaborators an Oscar

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:19.670
nomination for screenwriting.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:23.210
"This suit is black, purse, not"

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:28.740
In 2009, Baron Cohen brought his third and
final character, Bruno, to movie audiences,

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:31.380
but he was unable to recapture the magic of
Borat.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:36.460
Bruno, a mockumentary about an openly gay,
fashion-obsessed Austrian weirdo seriously

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:40.820
underperformed, bringing in less than half
of what Borat did and undoubtedly slowing

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.130
down Baron Cohen’s rise to fame.

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:44.860
Breakthrough dramatic role

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:49.130
In 2010, it was announced that Baron Cohen
was considering starring as singer Freddie

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:54.530
Mercury — to whom he certainly bears a resemblance
— in a biopic about the late Queen frontman.

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:59.040
Baron Cohen was actively involved in trying
to get the movie off the ground, even consulting

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:02.340
major directors like David Fincher and Tom
Hooper.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:06.730
But in 2013, he decided to pull out of the
project — and the film still hasn't been

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:07.730
made.

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:11.260
The actor claims he left the project because
the surviving members of Queen wanted the

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:14.900
movie to be a relatively tame biopic about
the entire band.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:19.480
On the other hand, Baron Cohen wanted it to
be purely a Freddie Mercury movie showcasing

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.230
the late rock star's wild life.

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:26.030
Queen guitarist Brian May offered a different
opinion on the issue, suggesting that Baron

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:30.260
Cohen would have be a distraction, as he doubted
that the larger-than-life actor could actually

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:33.160
disappear into the role and do it justice.

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:34.160
What's next?

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:37.930
Well, we likely haven't heard the last of
Sacha Baron Cohen and it wouldn’t be surprising

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:40.600
if he’s working on another big character
right now.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:44.720
From what we do know, Cohen has two main projects
in works the for the next few years.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:49.070
The first is a timely bit of satire called
Greed, in which he plays a money-mad, financial

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:50.470
law-skirting billionaire.

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:54.870
The other is a big-budget film adaptation
of Mandrake the Magician, in which he'll star

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:58.350
as the title character, a heroic master of
illusion.

00:04:58.350 --> 00:04:59.350
Seems like a good fit…

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:01.010
Thanks for watching!

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:04.130
